## The first run of this check, on the build before the fixes (18:08 to 18:09)
Airplane mode on at 18:08:27: the download stopped and showed waiting after three failed tries (18:08:34),
but NetworkState still said online: onLost asked Android for the active network and got the one being torn down.
Airplane mode off at 18:09:02: the download stayed waiting for 20 s and more, because the wait between tries
ended only on a change of the 'usable' flag, which never changed. Both were fixed (NetworkWatch.onLost reports
offline; any network change ends the wait; losing the network cuts the open connection at once) and the check run again above.
